		\label{prop:1.7}
		Let $p > 1$ and $q$ be the conjugate of $p$. Let $V \hookrightarrow H \hookrightarrow V^{*}$ be a Gelfand triple, where $V$ is a separable reflexive Banach space, $V^{*}$ is its strong dual and $H$ a separable Hilbert space with dense injections. Let $M$ be an $H$-valued $L^{2}$-integrable continuous martingale whose paths belong P-a.s. to $L^{p}(0, T ; V )$ and with $M(0) = 0$.\par
