		We pass to the limit in \eqref{eq:1.24} term by term. It remains to treat the stochastic integral for fixed $j$. 
		\par
		Let $\mathcal{P}_{T}$ denote the class of predictable processes with values in $L^{2}(\Omega_{T}; L_{Q}(H_{0,g}; H_{g}))$ with inner product given by
		\begin{equation}
			\label{eq:1.25}
			(G,J)_{\mathcal{P}_{T}} = \textbf{E}\int_{0}^{T} tr\{G(s)QJ^{*}(s)\}ds \quad \forall \,G,J \in \mathcal{P}_{T}.
